WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:04.042
♫La, la, la, la, la, la, la, la, la

00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:07.433
♫La, la, la, la, la, la

00:00:07.433 --> 00:00:08.908
- [Voiceover] What month did
you say your birthday was?

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:09.790
- In June.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.206
It's like June 18th, yeah.

00:00:11.206 --> 00:00:12.089
- [Voiceover] Okay.

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:12.971
- What is going on?

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:15.036
What is this video about?

00:00:15.036 --> 00:00:18.555
(funky music)

00:00:18.555 --> 00:00:19.755
- [Voiceover] Suppose you
were born in September.

00:00:19.755 --> 00:00:20.715
That would mean your birthday would come

00:00:20.715 --> 00:00:22.362
just after the cut-off
date for most schools

00:00:22.362 --> 00:00:24.139
in the United States.

00:00:24.139 --> 00:00:26.194
So if you were 15 on September first,

00:00:26.194 --> 00:00:28.214
you would play for the 15 year old team,

00:00:28.214 --> 00:00:30.536
even if you were turning 16 on the second.

00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:32.115
Studies have shown that this age gap

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:34.123
can give you an advantage,
because on average

00:00:34.123 --> 00:00:36.979
you're bigger and stronger
than the younger competition.

00:00:36.979 --> 00:00:39.822
This is called the relative age effect.

00:00:41.932 --> 00:00:44.525
Does being born in September
make you better at sports?

00:00:44.525 --> 00:00:46.741
I'm here at BuzzFeed to find out.

00:00:46.741 --> 00:00:48.089
- Patrick was bad at sports.

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:49.799
- (laughs) Kinda, I mean kinda.

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:50.667
I was kinda bad.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.745
- Well, I first broke my
nose while doing gymnastics,

00:00:52.745 --> 00:00:55.380
and then I broke it again,

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.394
because the basketball hit
me in the face in gym class.

00:00:58.394 --> 00:00:59.687
Maybe I'm not as athletic as I thought

00:00:59.687 --> 00:01:01.080
I was as a kid.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.658
- Oh, you know, you know what.

00:01:03.658 --> 00:01:04.923
I certainly wasn't the worst.

00:01:04.923 --> 00:01:07.848
I wasn't interested in being the best.

00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:10.170
If let's say there's 30 kids.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.842
I probably came up seventh.

00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:14.361
- Yeah, I was usually pretty,

00:01:14.361 --> 00:01:16.787
pretty high up on the

00:01:16.787 --> 00:01:19.388
skill level scale (laughs).

00:01:19.388 --> 00:01:20.688
I don't wanna sit here and be like,

00:01:20.688 --> 00:01:22.047
"I was the best at sports."

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:23.243
But I kinda was.

00:01:23.243 --> 00:01:26.621
- In high school I was
probably like a four or five.

00:01:26.621 --> 00:01:30.719
In elementary school I was
probably like a two or a three.

00:01:30.719 --> 00:01:34.179
but my heart level was like a 10,

00:01:34.179 --> 00:01:36.988
like I believed I could
do anything I wanted.

00:01:36.988 --> 00:01:40.100
- I was the team captain of
my high school tennis team.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.083
I was team captain of my squash team.

00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:45.488
I made varsity on football.

00:01:46.418 --> 00:01:49.213
I played rugby in
college for a while, too.

00:01:49.213 --> 00:01:50.931
- [Voiceover] I sent out a
survey to BuzzFeed employees

00:01:50.931 --> 00:01:53.137
to see what's the highest sports
team they ever played for.

00:01:53.137 --> 00:01:55.934
According to our study most
people quit after high school,

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.734
but we actually found that
there's three people here

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:59.395
that played professional sports.

00:01:59.395 --> 00:02:00.532
Two out of those three people

00:02:00.532 --> 00:02:03.216
were born in October and November.

00:02:03.216 --> 00:02:05.048
So, maybe your birthday
does have an effect,

00:02:05.048 --> 00:02:06.991
but we don't know for sure.

00:02:06.991 --> 00:02:11.892
(upbeat music)

